// Round 13 H2 (v0328 research ROUND13-ITEMS.md part H): every line of the law files under LAWS\UX, LAWS\DISTRIBUTION and
// LAWS\SYNC that begins "Automatic check:" (or "Automatic check on every push:", the form of LAWS\UX\U4.md), written as
// the line describes it and run against the five screens as built locally: the front door (/Knos/), the tool screen
// (/t/limit-check/), the result screen (/r/<id>/), the price screen (/Knos/pricing/, and the pay screen the tool shows
// when the free runs are used up) and the status page (/Knos/status/). The site and the app run locally (law_lib.mjs).
// DISTRIBUTION, SYNC and MISSION have no such line on 16 November 2026; UX has 159 (U1 25, U2 18, U3 18, U4 15, U5 21,
// U6 29, U7 33). Each check is labelled with its law file and line. A check whose subject is not on these screens (an
// Android app, a weekly job on live visitors' data) prints "n/a" with the reason and does not fail.
// A check fails with the value it measured. Thresholds are the ones the law line gives; none is made up here.
// KNOS_LAW_OUT=<file> writes every result as JSON (the R13 AUTO-CHECKS.csv is made from it).
